From 97dce5e8bb40d033465d0d0c6a2391c0ccdc6940 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: basalt-ink-experiments <noreply@localhost>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:32:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] inkling2: decode uses the prompt staging for RAM experts
 while no prompt is read (BASALT_INK_STAGING)

With BASALT_INK_ADAPT=1 and BASALT_INK_STAGING=1 the card memory the spilled layers share for the
prompt path's staging, idle during decode, holds the hottest RAM experts without a card buffer:
flat slots of the largest spilled blob, seen through the range whose tail maps all of the staging.
A round fills the free slots first (no card memory is taken) and the swaps may hand a slot on.
Before the prompt path reads (it writes the staging chunk by chunk) every staged expert's table
entry goes back to its RAM address on the session's stream, which is waited for; the next decode
window's round fills the slots again. Decode reads no other byte of the staging, the elastic
copy-back leaves staged experts alone, and the prompt path's staging from card copies counts the
copies only, as before.

Off by default.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
